{"title":"Natural transformation","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>natural transformation</b> is a way of turning one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functor\" title=\"Functor\">functor</a> into another functor while 'preserving' the structure of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Category_(category_theory)\" title=\"Category (category theory)\">categories</a>. Natural transformations can be thought of a 'morphisms between functors,' and indeed they are precisely the morphisms in functor categories.\n</p><p>More precisely, given two categories <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecbfb5e7dd547c1e0ca2eeb4669f2cc7f1ae4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36eee9eaded3a8c323d85046041a94a032ded392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{D}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, and two functors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/97636e4b0010ed0d2e48b41ecfbea5c4109c848e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F,G:\\mathcal{C}\\to \\mathcal{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />, then a natural transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8dd44a166d4e37bbea86c4d62290228ddd80225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi:F\\to G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> is a mapping which assigns to each object <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19dfccf74d999a047136f26cdb0752f5af6d445f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X\\in \\text{Ob}(\\mathcal{C})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> a morphism <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce9d472722deb05579bf70dce151d1d3ff00306d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi_X:F(X)\\to G(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36eee9eaded3a8c323d85046041a94a032ded392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{D}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> such that for every morphism <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a7f10cd1eb1a70f757d68726825511ffa17c6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:X\\to Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecbfb5e7dd547c1e0ca2eeb4669f2cc7f1ae4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />, we have:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240d371946d89b12baf5bf4eb56cc383a25648dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\varphi_Y\\circ F(f) = G(f)\\circ \\varphi_X.\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" />This equation can also be expressed by saying that the following diagram <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Commutative_diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Commutative diagram (page does not exist)\">commutes</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1291f5f2886e17b816ed45ca09d63e742e515c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((1.5,0)--(8.5,0),EndArrow); draw((1.5,10)--(8.5,10),EndArrow); draw((0,9)--(0,1),EndArrow); draw((10,9)--(10,1),EndArrow);  label(&quot;$G(f)$&quot;,(5,-1)); label(&quot;$F(f)$&quot;,(5,11)); label(&quot;$\\varphi_X$&quot;,(-1,5)); label(&quot;$\\varphi_Y$&quot;,(11,5));  label(&quot;$G(X)$&quot;,(0,0)); label(&quot;$G(Y)$&quot;,(10,0)); label(&quot;$F(X)$&quot;,(0,10)); label(&quot;$F(Y)$&quot;,(10,10)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"245\" />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Natural_transformation&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101102\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.081 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 307/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2384/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.859      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.859      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7238:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018101102 and revision id 27719. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}